1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,218
Every minute of a stroke, the brain can lose almost 2 million nerve cells.

2
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:10,559
A stroke happens when blood to part of the brain is blocked — or a vessel bursts.

3
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:14,938
B — Balance: sudden dizziness or trouble walking.

4
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:19,673
E — Eyes: sudden blurry, double, or lost vision.

5
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:23,054
F — Face: ask them to smile.

6
00:00:23,054 --> 00:00:24,343
Does one side droop?

7
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:27,498
A — Arms: raise both arms.

8
00:00:27,498 --> 00:00:28,843
Does one drift down?

9
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:32,490
S — Speech: is it slurred or strange?

10
00:00:34,750 --> 00:00:38,489
T — Time: call emergency services now, even if it fades.

11
00:00:38,489 --> 00:00:39,891
Note when it started.
